# Isolated git worktrees a session may create to work off the branch. They are
# a scratch checkout of this same repository, never source.
.claude/worktrees/

# =============================
#plan docs
#
# Excluded by default and opened per directory, never the reverse. The tree holds
# operational material beside the planning notes — probes that read a production
# connection string out of .env, deployment guides that name the certificate —
# and a blanket un-ignore would put access tooling in the history, where deleting
# it later does not remove it.
#
# What is opened below was audited file by file for credential VALUES rather than
# variable names: no connection string, no key, no certificate. The screenshots
# were opened and read; they carry placeholder figures, not a real balance.
# The contents are excluded, NOT the directory. `plan-docs/` on its own excludes
# the directory itself, so git never descends into it and no negation below can
# be reached — the re-includes would silently do nothing.
plan-docs/*
!plan-docs/ongoing/
!plan-docs/business-rules/
!plan-docs/completed/
# Crash dumps left behind when the Git Bash shell faults. Junk, and a hazard
# in a tree several sessions commit from: one careless "git add ." sweeps it in.
*.stackdump
